  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Tuesday)\nIssued at 148 AM CDT Wed Jun 10 2026\n\nHot temperatures are forecast on Thursday as an upper level ridge \ndominates the weather across West Central Texas. Highs will be in \nthe upper 90s to near 100 across most of the Big Country and in the \nmid to upper 90s elsewhere. Heat index values across portions of the \nBig Country will reach 101 to 104, which is just below Heat Advisory \ncriteria. Meanwhile, a cold front will move through the Great Plains \nlate Thursday, reaching north Texas during the evening hours. This \nfront may reach the northern portions of the Big Country Thursday \nnight into Friday morning. This will result in low to medium (20-\n40%) rain chances for the Big Country Thursday night into Friday.\nHighs on Friday will continue to hot, but a few degrees cooler \nthan forecast highs on Thursday. Expect afternoon highs in the mid\n90s. \n\nAs we head into the weekend and early next week, a broad upper level \ntrough will strengthen across the central CONUS late in the weekend, \nweakening the aforementioned upper level ridge. Until then, hot \ntemperatures will continue Saturday and Sunday with highs in the mid \n90s to near 100. A cold front will move through the area late Sunday \ninto Monday, ushering in cooler temperatures and bringing a chance of \nshowers and thunderstorms. The highest rain chances look to be \nSunday night into Monday when low to medium (30-60%) rain chances \nare forecast. Highs early next week will be in the mid 80s to lower \n90s.",
